Parent analysis 2026-10-07: Cost_tracker.sessions arithmetic rules it out as PRIMARY leak — each entry ~200B (4-field record + key string), sid is the stable session key (agent_turn_core.ml:51 passes turn-context sid), so cardinality is O(unique sessions/day)=dozens; 12.6MB/day needs ~60K entries/day. Registry still gets hygiene cleanup (tie to eviction) when the real leak is fixed. Pre-death signature: gc_major_blocks=516580 vs live_words=3.62M = avg 7 words/block — millions of TINY retained objects (strings/small records) from a high-volume source. Next: 11:15 hourly counters line (expect flat cost_sessions confirming rule-out) then Gc.Memprof census lane (OCaml 5.1 stdlib Gc.Memprof.start; SIGUSR1/config-triggered 30-min sampling window logging top allocation callstacks).

